c) · 5.32 KB\nL179: \nL180: 【70†Raw】\nL181: \nL182: Copy raw file\nL183: \nL184: Download raw file\nL185: \nL186: Outline\nL187: \nL188: Edit and raw actions\nL189: \nL190: # Changelog\nL191: \nL192: All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\nL193: \nL194: ## [Unreleased] — Canonical Rewrite\nL195: \nL196: Major revision: unified API, one verifier, one proof type, 7 provers, SIMD acceleration.\nL197: ### Breaking\nL198:   * Package renamed from `efficient-sumcheck` to `effsc`.\nL199:   * Single verifier — `sumcheck_verify()` returns `SumcheckResult { challenges, final_claim }`. The oracle check is the caller's responsibility (【71†Thaler Remark 4.2†people.cs.georgetown.edu】). Removed `inner_product_sumcheck_verify`, `multilinear_sumcheck_verify`, and `coefficient_sumcheck::sumcheck_verify`.\nL200:   * Single proof type — `SumcheckProof<F>` replaces `Sumcheck<F>` and `ProductSumcheck<F>`.\nL201:   * Transcript redesigned — `send()`/`receive()`/`challenge()` replace `read()`/`write()`.\nL202:   * Legacy entry points demoted — use `runner::sumcheck()` with a prover type.\nL203:   * Wire format: EvalsInfty. `d` values per round instead of `d + 1`; consistency is now structural. Details in 【72†docs/design.md §7a】.\nL204: ### Added\nL205:   * `SumcheckProver<F>` trait — single extension point for all polynomial shapes.\nL206:   * 7 concrete provers — `MultilinearProver`, `InnerProductProver`, `CoefficientProver` (each with MSB + LSB variants), `GkrProver`.\nL207:   * `SumcheckField` trait — generic field interface; blanket impl for `ark_ff::Field` behind `feature = \"arkworks\"`.\nL208:   * `SimdRepr` trait — safe SIMD opt-in with `zerocopy` layout verification.\nL209:   * `runner::sumcheck()` — single runner with partial execution and per-round hooks.\nL210:   * Eq polynomial utilities — `eq_poly`, `eq_poly_non_binary`, O(2^v) incremental `compute_hypercube_eq_evals`.\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------