deg_j(g) + 1) field elements. When deg_j(g) = O(1) for all j (the common case), this is O(v) field elements.\nL191: ### What the verifier checks\nL192: \nL193: Per round: one consistency equation (g_j(0) + g_j(1) = previous claim) and a degree bound (deg g_j <= deg_j(g)). After all rounds: one oracle query to g at a random point.\nL194: \nL195: Total verifier time: O(v + sum_j deg_j(g)) + T, where T is the cost of one evaluation of g at a point in F^v.\nL196: ## 2. Our three use cases are one protocol\nL197: \nL198: Thaler's protocol is parameterized by g. Our current three entry points are three instantiations:\nL199: \nL200: Use case  | g  | deg per var  | Ref\nL201: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL202: multilinear_sumcheck  | f_tilde (MLE of evals)  | 1  | §4.1\nL203: inner_product_sumcheck  | f_tilde * g_tilde  | 2  | §4.4\nL204: coefficient_sumcheck  | user-defined  | d  | §4.6\nL205: In all three cases, the protocol is identical — only the prover's round-polynomial computation changes. This motivates a single protocol runner parameterized by a prover trait, not three separate functions.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn2view4 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/compsec-epfl/efficient-sumcheck/blob/main/LICENSE-MIT\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://github.com/compsec-epfl/efficient-sumcheck/blob/main/LICENSE-MIT: Cache miss--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn2view5 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/snarang181/zk-duel/blob/master/LICENSE\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://github.com/snarang181/zk-duel/blob/master/LICENSE: Cache miss"
